  "summary_en": "Canada's Treasury Board Secretariat strategy for responsible AI adoption across the federal public service in 2025-2027. It sets a vision and four principles (human centred, collaborative, ready, responsible), priority areas including policy, legislation and governance, and expectations for departments. It has no robotics-specific provisions.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Four principles: human centred, collaborative, ready, responsible",
   "Priority area on policy, legislation and governance, with scheduled review cycles for AI-related law and policy",
   "Departments are expected to inform clients and public servants when and how AI is used",
   "Scope follows the OECD AI system definition and covers all lifecycle stages",
   "Public consultation found support for labelling AI content and no-go areas such as criminal justice and hiring decisions"
